{
  "title": "Serum protein gap modestly improves frozen cross-cycle prediction of log CRP beyond albumin and blood-count correlates",
  "abstract": "In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, adding serum total protein minus albumin to a frozen source-trained model of log CRP reduced target MEC-weighted MSE from 1.058677 to 1.022838 in the independently sampled 2007\u201308 cycle (n=4861); gain 0.035839, target-PSU 95% interval 0.021682\u20130.049857, conditional on the 2005\u201306 fit. This is modest within-program transfer of a known marker, not clinical validation or novel biology.",
